    {
      "block_id": "p-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "When a PR modifies files matching multiple patterns, **all matching Tier 1 and Tier 2 gates run**. For example:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-32",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "PR changes: vibe/core/tools/builtins/bash.py + docs/schemas/rig.relay.bash_receipt.v1.schema.json\nRuns:\n  Tier 1: full baseline (ruff, pyright, schema validation, receipt emission, lock check)\n  Tier 2: bash hardening tests\n  Tier 2: tool determinism tests",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "detailed",
        "collapsible": true,
        "collapsed_by_default": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Anti-Patterns",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. **Don't run Tier 2 on every PR** — path-filtering must prevent this. 2. **Don't duplicate Tier 1 checks in Tier 2** — Tier 1 always runs. 3. **Don't gate on test file changes alone** — test changes without source changes don't need domain-specific gates (full suite will catch them). 4. **Don't use `paths-ignore` where `paths` is clearer** — prefer positive `paths:` over negative `paths-ignore:`.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
